{"c":[{"id":"ff412afe096d8651","sum":"W3/B25: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply; MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory and grants no authority; oxc needs   escaped. Push v2/* only to sam. Intents gpt-oss-120b, plans qwen3.8 (~1k out tok/min); space writer calls with a fresh AbortSignal.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c539feeaf5360a4d","sum":"W3: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory (real folder only without --data-dir) and grants no authority (that stays in memory.sqlite). oxc rejects raw U+2028 in a regex; write \\u2028.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"569740c12f8fdab5","sum":"W3: client setCodeSigningRequirement blocks what it receives, not its first call; XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory is markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory; main.ts uses the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-a08d2817ff5ece3d","text":"W3: NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement on the client blocks what it receives, not its own first call; whoever owns the Mach name sees open's arguments, so XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204904Z-98cc6d5ebfceb30a","text":"Personal memory is markdown (helper/src/memory): MemoryStore(dir) keeps it in <dir>/Memory unless told otherwise, and main.ts uses ~/Library/Application Support/Caret/Memory only when --data-dir is not given, so tests and evals never open the real folder.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6e639a4926698b7e","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (permissions, onItsOwn, hand-off stay in memory.sqlite); editing a skill file puts it back on Tab (SkillJson.fileDigest). oxc rejects a raw U+2028/U+2029 in a regex literal; write the \\u2028 escape (Write tools may unescape it).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204920Z-024f4219fb18c6cf","text":"Memory markdown grants no authority: permissions and a skill's onItsOwn, clean runs and hand-off stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill's file puts it back on Tab, and SkillJson.fileDigest catches edits made while Caret was stopped.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204920Z-0ba29fff62387456","text":"vite's oxc parser rejects a regex literal holding a raw U+2028/U+2029 (a line terminator); write the \\u2028 escape. An agent's Write tool can turn the escape into the raw character.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e60e3e751e2435c2","sum":"Remotes and Groq writers: push v2/* only to remote sam; Ask intents use gpt-oss-120b, plan programs qwen3.8 (about 1,000 output tokens a minute and 200k a day); space writer calls with a fresh AbortSignal after each wait. U+2731 marks required labels on the job form.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e2ebd6c0099fdfde","sum":"Push v2/* only to remote sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret); origin is the team hackathon repo. Ask intents use INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8, ~1,000 output tokens/min, 200k/day on Groq); gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T210855Z-22a0908ac8155d26","text":"Push v2/* branches to the remote named sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret), where their PRs live. origin is the team hackathon repo (theodorexli/hackathon-2026-09-19); a bare 'git push origin' publishes there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-2bd567d78f578d5c","text":"B25: Ask intents go to INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs to WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8); qwen3.8's Groq 200k tokens/day ran out during dev runs, and gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400 'does not match the expected schema'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b1d476e32a92cb95","sum":"B25: writers that space calls must give each request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait (a 15 s gap aborted every call); the job form marks required labels with U+2731, which realfill normLabel strips.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-3925313f151b5275","text":"B25: eval writers that space calls must give the request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait; a 15 s gap aborted every intent in planner-eval's first GUI run.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-9174d67891bff255","text":"B25: the job form marks required labels with U+2731; realfill normLabel strips it, and B24's scoreboards counted those four fields as not found.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0039d51d111ccafa","sum":"B25-B26/D2-02: never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; bridge sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; Ask sentences in planner/says.ts; Jev 'confidence' is the top-two margin; Groq gpt-oss-120b allows 8k tok/min (space Ask evals 30 s); a one-token Groq probe hides a spent day.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"97c4b1112eed6f12","sum":"B25/W4/B26: never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; captcha frames via compose.ts unit tests; bridge sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; a one-token Groq probe hides a spent day.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e7d7ded421a71b5d","sum":"B25/W4: never-typed kinds live only in memory/sensitive.ts (extend it, no second list). HSTS-preloaded captcha hosts can't be pointed at a local server; test captcha frames via extension/src/worker/compose.ts unit tests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-bc8230171f42cb4e","text":"B25: never-typed kinds (fill, planner, Ask) are memory/sensitive.ts, M1's classifier copied unchanged from v2/memory; extend that file, never a second list.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220624Z-f865060dd10d04a3","text":"W4: hcaptcha/recaptcha hosts are HSTS-preloaded, so --host-resolver-rules cannot point a test browser's captcha frame at a local http server (the load hangs); test captcha frame composition through extension/src/worker/compose.ts unit tests instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1c32ace5fe4e098f","sum":"W4/B26: bridge test sockets a fixture accept()s need SO_NOSIGPIPE or signal 13 kills the run. Groq answers a one-token probe after a model's daily tokens run out; only a real-size request shows the 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T223033Z-e64c70b59e406a7f","text":"W4: Swift Testing runs bridge tests in one process; a test socket that a fixture accept()s needs SO_NOSIGPIPE, or a write after the peer closed kills the whole run with signal 13, blamed on whichever test was running.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-04a43869ad872043","text":"B26: Groq answers a one-token probe even when a model's tokens-per-day is spent; only a real-size request shows the 429 TPD. gpt-oss-120b's day ran out during B26's first Ask run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"78eeba3d0e4f7ab9","sum":"B26/D2-02: Ask sentences live in planner/says.ts; generator measurements pin setGeneratorClock; Jev 'confidence' is the top-two margin; Groq gpt-oss-120b allows 8k tokens/min, so Ask evals space calls 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"943dffc1dbc84f96","sum":"B26: Ask refusals and questions live in planner/says.ts (SaidError message for the user, detail for ids and provider errors); offline generator measurements must pin setGeneratorClock or cold forms hit the time budget.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T224111Z-32ca3d0fc6e98438","text":"B26: every Ask refusal or question sentence lives in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads and its detail holds the check's text (ids, provider errors). Scoreboards print both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-6a820f7b64075f54","text":"B26: offline generator measurements (scripts/realfill-budgets.ts and the like) must pin setGeneratorClock, or cold first forms are cut short by the time budget and the numbers vary run to run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"47481f5f6fb24ec8","sum":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the top-two margin (0.75 needs ~0.875 on the winner); Groq gpt-oss-120b, the Ask intent writer, allows 8,000 tokens/min, so Ask evals space calls 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233505Z-310484d235184787","text":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the margin between the top two option probabilities (raw answers also carry 'probabilities'); a 0.75 floor needs about 0.875 on the winner.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233506Z-254786afcaf981c8","text":"D2-02: Groq gpt-oss-120b (the Ask intent writer) allows 8,000 tokens a minute; an intent is about 2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429 'unavailable'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
